Hi,

   I would avoid using bootstrap.  Bootstrap was pretty common a few years 
ago, but there are some theoretial results that suggest that bootstrap may 
not be reliable (see Abadie and Imbens' recent article in Econometrica). 
Also, from a practical perspective, you can condition your inference on 
the matched-sample and make your inference. See Section 6.9 of our paper: 
http://imai.princeton.edu/research/files/matchp.pdf

Best,
Kosuke

